  "description": "A parametric OUTDOOR LIGHT on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nTHE SPILL IS THE DRAWING. A bollard is 140 mm of nothing in plan; what a lighting layout needs is the pool it throws, so the spill is a 32-point ring at floor level on its own pale slot — visible while setting out, switched off for the final sheet.\n\nTHE PUBLISHED SPACING is 1.7 × the spill radius, which is the overlap that gives an even wash along a path rather than a row of separate puddles. It is the number this object exists to answer.\n\nTHREE STYLES ON THE HEAD'S HEIGHT. A Bollard hangs its head at the top of a post so the mount height is the head's top; a Wall light drops the post for a bracket and takes the mount height as the head's underside; Post top is a bollard at any height. One ternary, one object.",
